# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets _headers file.
# Lives at the ASSETS ROOT (copied to dist-cf/_headers by build:cf — NOT under
# public/, which would nest it under /apps/filemark/ where CF ignores it).
# Path patterns match the request URL the worker sees, i.e. /apps/filemark/*.
#
# Scope note: deliberately NO Strict-Transport-Security or Content-Security-
# Policy here — HSTS is domain-wide and belongs to the parent khanakia.com
# gateway, and a wrong CSP would break GTM / inline scripts. These four are
# safe, universally-recommended hardening headers.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

# Hashed build assets are content-addressed — cache them forever.
/apps/filemark/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The YouTube embed helper (embed/youtube.html) exists SPECIFICALLY to be framed
# cross-origin: filemark's non-web hosts (Chrome extension `chrome-extension://`,
# VS Code webview `vscode-webview://`, `file://`) iframe it so YouTube receives a
# valid https Referer and plays (works around YouTube's Error 153). The site-wide
# `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` above would forbid that framing, so drop it for
# this path so ANY embedder can frame it. The page only wraps a public YouTube
# video — no auth, cookies, or secrets — so unrestricted framing is safe here.
#
# Why no `frame-ancestors` allow-list at all:
#   • `frame-ancestors *` fails — `*` matches only NETWORK schemes
#     (http/https/ws/wss), so `chrome-extension://` is still blocked.
#   • `frame-ancestors https: chrome-extension: vscode-webview: file:` fixes the
#     Chrome extension, but the VS Code webview embeds from a SANDBOXED / OPAQUE
#     (null) origin, and CSP has NO token that can allowlist a null origin — so
#     it stays blocked no matter what schemes are listed.
# The only way to permit an opaque-origin embedder is to send no framing
# restriction at all: drop X-Frame-Options and set no frame-ancestors. That
# leaves the page framable everywhere, which is acceptable for this one path.
/apps/filemark/embed/*
  ! X-Frame-Options
